<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 md:px-12" aria-labelledby="questions-heading">
  <div class="border-t border-border-light py-12">
    <h2 id="questions-heading" class="mb-6 font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">A few things to know</h2>
    <details class="border-b border-border-light py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer py-1 font-medium">Does everything stay on my computer?</summary>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-text-tertiary">OpenWaggle stores session data locally. Requests to hosted AI models send messages and code outside your computer. Connected tools can send data too. See <a class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4" href="/docs/configuration/security-privacy">privacy and data</a> for details.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="border-b border-border-light py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer py-1 font-medium">Do I need to run multiple agents?</summary>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-text-tertiary">No. You can work with one agent in a normal conversation. Waggle and Hives are optional.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="border-b border-border-light py-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer py-1 font-medium">Can I use my existing provider account?</summary>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-text-tertiary">Authentication options depend on the provider. Some support signing in through your browser; others require an API key. Check <a class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4" href="/docs/providers/overview">provider setup</a> for the available connections.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
